/*Singleton Design Pattern ensures only one instance of a class is created and provides a global access point to that instance.
        The best way to implement Singleton is using Double Locking Mechanism or Enum Singleton.

        Singleton is primarily a Creational Design Pattern, but in rare cases like Logging Service or Caching, it can also
        act as a Behavioral Design Pattern because it manages global communication between objects.

        how to create Singleton class in java
        1.> private constructor
        2.> static variable
        3.> static method

        we can create three ways singleton  object
        1.> EagerInitialization(Thread-safe+simple)
        2.> lazyInitialization: Object created when it required (not thread safe+slow)
        3.> Double locking (thread safe + performance)

        why we use Singleton design pattern
           when you want to restrict the object creation to only one instance for:
           1.>Database connection Pools
           2.>Logging
           3.>Cache memory
           4.>Configuration files

           reflection,Cloning will break singleton because it will create duplicate objects so to avoid that we need to use
           Enum Singleton

         */
